  "summary": "Coralville, Iowa removed its Flock ALPR cameras after the city council voted 3-1 to terminate the contract, rather than comply with an Iowa Attorney General order to strip an anti-ICE stipulation from its policy. The original policy barred using Flock data for immigration enforcement; the AG said that violated state law preempting local interference with immigration enforcement.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the Iowa Attorney General's Office sent a letter to the city stating its Flock camera policy was in violation of Iowa law. That law prohibits local entities from impeding immigration enforcement.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Rather than amend the policy, the city council voted on a resolution to stop using the cameras entirely.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock will not be used on the sole basis to enforce immigration law. So if ICE is requesting access to our data, it's a no,",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "The council voted 3 to 1 to terminate the contract with Flock and discontinue use of its cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
  ],
